xtension `agent_end`. `scheduleMaybeContinueGoal()` uses a 25ms timer and only checks active goal, `ctx.isIdle()`, pending messages, and safety caps. Pi extension `ctx.isIdle()` is bound to `!this.isStreaming` and does not include `isCompacting`; thus continuation can fire during compaction or skip once with no post-compaction retry. Pi threshold compaction with `willRetry=false` only continues if agent has queued messages, and a pi-goals direct `triggerTurn` continuation while not streaming may not be in that queue. Desired fix: compaction-aware continuation handling in pi-goals: listen to `session_before_compact`/`session_compact`, track compaction-in-progress, suppress/reroute continuation while compacting, and after successful `session_compact` schedule continuation for an active goal with a new reason such as `compacted`; add telemetry/skip reason for compaction suppression. Mention possible Pi core companion: `ctx.isIdle()` should include compaction or expose `ctx.isCompacting()`. Required proofs should include deterministic race/order probe (`agent_end -&gt; session_before_compact -&gt; session_compact` leads to exactly one post-compaction continuation), suppression probe (no send while compaction flag active), quality gate `npm run quality:goal`, and bounded live probe or explicit skip reason. Grounded files include `.pi/extensions/goal/continuation.ts`, `.pi/extensions/goal/lifecycle.ts`, `.pi/extensions/goal/types.ts`, `.pi/extensions/goal/telemetry.ts`, Pi docs `docs/compaction.md`, `docs/extensions.md`, and Pi core `dist/core/agent-session.js` lines around `_processAgentEvent`, `_checkCompaction`, `_runAutoCompaction`, `sendCustomMessage`, and context bindings.&lt;/context&gt;\n&lt;/issue_request&gt;\n\nUse `$feature-workflow-pipelines` as the governing workflow. If the task touches agent-facing CLI ergonomics, also use `$axi`. If the task is architecture-sensitive, use `$sentrux` as a planning/quality sensor where appropriate.\n\nMandatory protocol-read